* {{cog|ang|ǣht|t=livestock; property; possession; power}}
* {{cog|goh|frēht|t=earnings}} (modern {{cog|de|fracht}})
* {{cog|sv|frakt}}
{{rel-bottom}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun|-|s}} {{term-label|en|obsolete|also|figurative}}

# {{lb|en|nautical}}
## The [[hire#Noun|hire]] of a [[boat#Noun|boat]] or [[ship#Noun|ship]] to [[transport#Verb|transport]] [[cargo]].
## [[money#Noun|Money]] [[pay#Verb|paid]] to [[hire#Verb|hire]] a [[vessel#Noun|vessel]] for this [[purpose#Noun|purpose]]; [[freight#Noun|freight]].
##: {{hyponyms|en|boatage|shippage<q:dated>}}
##: {{ux|en|'''fraught''' money}}
## The [[transportation]] of [[goods]], especially in a boat or ship.
##: {{hyponyms|en|boatage|shippage<q:dated>}}
## A ship's cargo; freight, [[lading#Noun|lading]].
##* {{RQ:Marlowe Jew of Malta|I|text=Well, go, / And bid the merchants and my men despatch, / And come ashore, and see the '''fraught''' discharg'd.}}
##* {{quote-book|en|year=1596|author=w:William Shakespeare; {{w|Thomas Kyd}} ''(uncertain)''|title=[[w:Edward III (play)|Edward III]]|section=act III, scene iv|url=https://archive.org/stream/cu31924013134337|passage={{...}} And now behold after my winters toyle, / My paynefull voyage on the boyſtrous ſea, / Of warres deuouring gulphes and ſteely rocks, / I bring my '''fraught''' vnto the wiſhed port / My Summers hope, my trauels ſweet reward {{...}}}}
